# Content Data Authoring

## Card assets (authoring surface)

Create via `Assets → Create → BPD/Content/Card Definition`, then add to a deck
(`Assets → Create → BPD/Content/Card Deck`).

Paths:
- Cards: `Assets/Resources/Content/Cards/SO_Card_*.asset`
- Decks: `Assets/Resources/Content/Decks/SO_Deck_Default.asset`
- Menu: `BPD → Content → Seed Default Card Deck` (recreates PLACEHOLDER stubs)

### Required fields

| Field | Purpose |
|-------|---------|
| `Id` | Stable id (`card_stub_001`) |
| `SituationText` | Event / situation copy (PLACEHOLDER ok) |
| `LeftActionName` + `LeftEffects` | Left swipe label + Wholeness/Stability/Safety/Closeness deltas |
| `RightActionName` + `RightEffects` | Right swipe label + deltas |
| `LeftTriggersLose` / `RightTriggersLose` | Force Split when that choice is applied |
| `AllowSkill` | Show skill resolution on this card |
| `RequiredSkill` | `DbtSkillId` gate (`None` = any unlocked charge) |
| `SkillActionName` + `SkillEffects` | Skill button label + deltas |

Runtime still applies through `CardChoice` / `StatDelta[]` via `CardDefinition.Left|Right|SkillChoice`.

## DBT skill assets

Create via `Assets → Create → BPD/Content/DBT Skill`. Optional overrides under:

- `Assets/Resources/Content/Skills/SO_Skill_*.asset`

Built-in catalog covers every `DbtSkillId` if assets are missing (`DbtSkillCatalog`).

Fields: `Id`, `DisplayName`, `Module`, `Description`, `ChargesOnUnlock`, `IsProductive`.

Unlock only via Split survive (`SplitSkillRewards`) or Therapy Need `SkillUnlockId`.

## Placeholders

- Stub ids: `card_stub_001`, `therapy_stub_situation_01`, etc.
- Mark unfinished copy/balance with `PLACEHOLDER` in text or ids.
- Humans replace stubs via GDD / Google Sheets export — do not invent final narrative.

## Localization

- MVP: PLACEHOLDER copy may live on the card SO (content asset, not gameplay C#).
- Skill educational text may live in catalog builtins / SO.
- Later Sheets pass: move final EN/RU into locale tables; keep SO ids stable.
- Never hardcode player-facing English inside gameplay systems (controllers/services).

## Canon

See `Docs/Canon-Mechanics.md` for Split-at-Zero, XP+deck level win, endings, and skill unlock rules.
